 "summary": "Gurevich's model of computation (originally 'evolving algebras') in which a state is a first-order structure and a program is a set of guarded function updates fired in parallel; Börger's ASM method uses it for stepwise-refined system specification, executed by tools such as ASMETA (AsmetaL), CoreASM and Microsoft's AsmL.",
 "status": "maintained",
